<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Do Muoi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–2018</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Đỗ Mười</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Do Muoi was a Vietnamese communist leader who served as prime minister from 1988 to 1991 and as general secretary of the Communist Party from 1991 to 1997. He continued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doi-moi">Doi Moi</a> market reforms while keeping the party's monopoly of power, and during his leadership <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> normalised relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/association-of-southeast-asian-nations">ASEAN</a> in 1995.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/do-muoi.jpg" alt="Do Muoi" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I myself cropped, original author is Lưu Ly at vi.wikipedia.org · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Do_Muoi_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
